   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROGRESS REPORT ON YOUTH IN HORTICULTURE</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organized from the 3rd to the 12th of November in Accra, the program commenced with training sessions and team exercises covering email etiquette, pitching skills, networking in professional settings, and building a strong online professional brand. Through Belbin&apos;s test, participants gained insights into their strengths and weaknesses within a team, enhancing their ability to complement each other effectively.

The subsequent day included a visit to Holland Greentech for practical training sessions, introducing participants to hydroponics, sustainable cultivation techniques, and best farming practices by the Defarmercist. The day concluded with a visit to a greenhouse farm owned by Farmer Nii.

In the following days, teams visited participating companies, Eden Tree Limited and Farm Estates Limited, to grasp the context of their business challenges and work on their solutions. The program also featured sessions with established entrepreneurs, providing participants with opportunities to network and draw inspiration from their journey and success stories. Additionally, an online session with experts from PUM introduced participants to the Dutch horticulture landscape.

Throughout the program, dedicated coaches were available to help participants navigate team dynamics and provide guidance on crafting effective solutions and professional development.</narrative>
   </description>
